<title>FRANCE: France sees 97 grain sowings up three pct.</title>
<headline>France sees 97 grain sowings up three pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's farm ministry said on Wednesday that total grain sowings for the 1997 harvest may rise by three percent over the previous year to 9.093 million hectares.</p>
<p>In its first estimate for the 1997 maize harvest, the ministry put maize area at 1.749 million hectares, up 1.2 percent over 1996.</p>
<p>It also revised down its estimate for soft wheat sowings to 4.923 million hectares from 4.930 million hectares forecast last month. This would represent a rise of 3.2 percent over area sown in 1996.  </p>
<p>In a monthly report, the ministry's SCEES statistical office</p>
<p>gave the following main sowing projections, effective May 1.</p>
<p>			   Hectares ('000)  Yr/yr change</p>
<p>			    ('000)		(percent)</p>
<p>    Total grain	 9,093		    3.0</p>
<p>    Soft wheat	  4,923		    3.2</p>
<p>    Barley		1,625		    6.2</p>
<p>    Oats		    135		   -4.1</p>
<p>    Rye			47		   -2.0</p>
<p>    Triticale	     204		    0.0</p>
<p>    Maize		 1,749		    1.2</p>
<p>    Sorghum		  65		   19.3</p>
</text>
